# samples/07-OpenApiImport – start it with: dotnet run --project samples/07-OpenApiImport
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5107

### Mock: the documented example of listPets
GET {{baseUrl}}/pets

### Mock: the example with {{petId}} rendered
GET {{baseUrl}}/pets/7

### Mock: 201 with the example, {{name}} and {{species}} from the request
POST {{baseUrl}}/pets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Polly", "species": "bird" }

### 400 – species is an enum in the document
POST {{baseUrl}}/pets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nemo", "species": "fish" }

### x-dynamic-endpoints-processor: the "inventory" processor, even in mock mode
GET {{baseUrl}}/store/inventory

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/store/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "petId": 1, "quantity": 2 }

### Re-import version 2 with sync – dry run: update, create, delete, unchanged
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/import/openapi?mock=true&mode=sync&enabled=true&dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json

< ./petstore-v2.json

### …for real
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/import/openapi?mock=true&mode=sync&enabled=true
Content-Type: application/json

< ./petstore-v2.json

### New in version 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/pets/1/photos

### A processor per tag (not a mock), under a route prefix – dry run
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/import/openapi?processor=echo&processorByTag=store:echo&routePrefix=/v1&dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json

< ./petstore.json

### Options in the body: { document, options } – configurations don't fit in a query string
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints/import/openapi?dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "document": { "openapi": "3.0.3", "info": { "title": "Tiny", "version": "1" },
                "paths": { "/ping": { "get": { "operationId": "ping", "tags": ["health"], "responses": { "200": { "description": "pong" } } } } } },
  "options": {
    "routePrefix": "/tiny",
    "processorsByTag": { "health": { "processor": "response", "processorConfig": { "body": { "pong": true } } } }
  }
}

### The imported endpoints – each records its origin
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints
